From 1a371dda83a1e34463f207a6768d00d8483f1123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Meumertzheim <fabian@meumertzhe.im>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:24:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Pass server JVM arguments via an argfile on Windows

In batch mode, the client passes its entire environment to the server JVM as --client_env arguments, which can exceed the 32,767-character command-line limit of CreateProcessW.

Always pass server JVM arguments through a Java launcher argfile instead of estimating whether the command line fits. The launcher expands it before the JVM starts, and the temporary file is removed after the JVM exits.

Fixes #31376

RELNOTES: None

Upstream PR: https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/31380
---
